{
 "Actor, Judge, or Teacher? · REAL Lab Blog": "Actor, Judge, or Teacher? · REAL Lab 博客",
 "Decision models such as JEV struggle to act on tasks whose subgoals must be met in order, yet judged in hindsight they teach a 1.5B policy that outperforms them: 72.8% → 82.9% on ALFWorld and 56.8% → 71.4% on WebShop.": "JEV 等决策模型独立执行时，在子目标有先后顺序的任务上常出错；但在回合结束后为每个动作评分时，由它指导训练的 1.5B 策略反而超过它本身。与仅用 GRPO 相比，ALFWorld 成功率由 72.8% 提升至 82.9%，WebShop 由 56.8% 提升至 71.4%。",
 "A decision model that acts poorly can still teach well, if it is asked whether each action helped and shown the whole trajectory.": "决策模型独立执行时常出错，却可以成为有效的教师。前提是提问恰当：询问每个动作是否有助于达成目标，并提供完整轨迹。",
 "<a href=\"../../blog.html\">Blog</a><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>November 22, 2026</span><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>Agentic AI · Reinforcement learning</span><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>14 min read</span>": "<a href=\"../../blog.html\">博客</a><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>2026 年 11 月 22 日</span><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>智能体 · 强化学习</span><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>阅读约 14 分钟</span>",
 "Decision models answer a question with a choice and a probability, so the same model can pick an agent's actions, grade them, or teach a policy. We find that a model which acts poorly can still teach well, as long as it is asked the right question and shown the whole trajectory.": "决策模型针对问题给出一个选项及各选项的概率，因此同一模型有三种用法：为智能体选择动作，即执行者（Actor）；为动作评分，即裁判（Judge）；指导策略训练，即教师（Teacher）。本文发现，独立执行时常出错的模型同样可以成为有效的教师，前提是提问恰当，并提供完整轨迹。",
 "<sup>1</sup>Zhejiang University <sup>2</sup>Baidu Inc. · *Equal contribution †Corresponding author": "<sup>1</sup>浙江大学 <sup>2</sup>百度 · *同等贡献 †通讯作者",
 "<a href=\"#roles\"><span class=\"n\">1</span>Three ways to ask</a>": "<a href=\"#roles\"><span class=\"n\">1</span>同一模型的三种用法</a>",
 "<a href=\"#actor\"><span class=\"n\">2</span>As an actor</a>": "<a href=\"#actor\"><span class=\"n\">2</span>作为执行者</a>",
 "<a href=\"#actor-order\">Ordered subgoals</a>": "<a href=\"#actor-order\">有先后顺序的子目标</a>",
 "<a href=\"#actor-distract\">Distraction, not ignorance</a>": "<a href=\"#actor-distract\">错误源于干扰而非能力不足</a>",
 "<a href=\"#judge\"><span class=\"n\">3</span>As a judge</a>": "<a href=\"#judge\"><span class=\"n\">3</span>作为裁判</a>",
 "<a href=\"#judge-question\">Ask about the action</a>": "<a href=\"#judge-question\">评估动作贡献而非任务成败</a>",
 "<a href=\"#judge-context\">Show the whole trajectory</a>": "<a href=\"#judge-context\">提供完整轨迹</a>",
 "<a href=\"#teacher\"><span class=\"n\">4</span>As a teacher</a>": "<a href=\"#teacher\"><span class=\"n\">4</span>作为教师</a>",
 "<a href=\"#teacher-signal\">From scores to advantages</a>": "<a href=\"#teacher-signal\">从评分到优势</a>",
 "<a href=\"#teacher-results\">Results</a>": "<a href=\"#teacher-results\">实验结果</a>",
 "<a href=\"#teacher-surpass\">Learning beyond the teacher</a>": "<a href=\"#teacher-surpass\">学生超过教师</a>",
 "<a href=\"#takeaways\"><span class=\"n\">5</span>Takeaways</a>": "<a href=\"#takeaways\"><span class=\"n\">5</span>启示</a>",
 "<a href=\"#roles\">Three ways to ask a decision model</a>": "<a href=\"#roles\">同一模型的三种用法</a>",
 "<a href=\"#actor\">As an actor</a>": "<a href=\"#actor\">作为执行者</a>",
 "<a href=\"#judge\">As a judge</a>": "<a href=\"#judge\">作为裁判</a>",
 "<a href=\"#teacher\">As a teacher</a>": "<a href=\"#teacher\">作为教师</a>",
 "<a href=\"#takeaways\">Takeaways</a>": "<a href=\"#takeaways\">启示</a>",
 "A <em>decision model</em> answers a question about a context with a typed output, such as a choice among options with a probability for each, instead of free text. Because any question can be asked about any state, one model can choose an agent's next action, evaluate an action already taken, or score every action of a policy during reinforcement learning. So far these models have mostly been judged by how well they act.": "<em>决策模型</em>不输出自由文本，而是针对给定上下文回答问题，答案格式固定，例如从若干选项中选出一个，并给出各选项的概率。问题与状态可以任意组合，因此同一模型既能为智能体选择下一步动作，也能评估已执行的动作，还能在强化学习中为策略的每个动作评分。然而，现有工作评价这类模型时，主要关注其独立执行的表现。",
 "We asked whether a model that acts poorly can still teach well. On ALFWorld, JEV completes <strong>42.9%</strong> of tasks when it chooses the actions itself. Used instead to score each action of a 1.5B policy during GRPO training, it raises that policy's success over GRPO alone from 72.8% to <strong>82.9%</strong> on the same tasks, and from 56.8% to <strong>71.4%</strong> on WebShop. <strong>The difference comes from timing: an actor must anticipate consequences, whereas a judge that reads the finished episode can see them.</strong>": "本文关注的问题是：独立执行表现差的模型，能否成为好的教师？在 ALFWorld 上，JEV 独立选择动作时仅完成 <strong>42.9%</strong> 的任务；而在 GRPO 训练中由它为 1.5B 策略的每个动作评分时，策略在同一批任务上的成功率由单用 GRPO 的 72.8% 提升至 <strong>82.9%</strong>，在 WebShop 上则由 56.8% 提升至 <strong>71.4%</strong>。<strong>差异来自评估时机：执行者只能事先预判后果，裁判评估的是已经结束的回合，后果已经可见。</strong>",
 "The benefit is not automatic. It appears only when the model is asked whether each action <em>helped achieve the goal</em>, rather than whether the task will succeed, and only when it sees the <em>whole trajectory</em> rather than the steps leading up to the action. Queried this way after each episode, a frozen decision model provides step-level supervision for 22 to 30 USD of API calls per training run, with no step labels and no learned critic.": "这一收益有前提条件。提问须针对每个动作<em>是否有助于达成目标</em>，而非任务能否成功；提供的上下文须为<em>完整轨迹</em>，而非该动作之前的若干步。按此方式在每个回合结束后提问，参数冻结的决策模型即可提供步级监督，既无需步级标注，也无需训练 critic，每次训练的 API 费用仅为 22 至 30 美元。",
 "<span class=\"n\">1</span>Three ways to ask a decision model": "<span class=\"n\">1</span>同一模型的三种用法",
 "A decision model takes a <em>question</em> and a <em>context</em>. For a multiple-choice question it selects an option and assigns a probability to every option; for a yes/no question it returns one score in [0, 1]. We query the same model in three roles that differ only in what it is asked and how its answer is used.": "决策模型的输入包括<em>问题</em>与<em>上下文</em>两部分。对于选择题，模型选出一个选项，并给出各选项的概率；对于是非题，模型返回 [0, 1] 区间内的分数。以下三种角色使用同一模型，区别仅在于提问内容与回答的用途。",
 "<span class=\"role-a\">Actor.</span> At each step the model picks the next action from the valid commands, given the goal, the history and the current observation. The choice is executed.": "<span class=\"role-a\">执行者（Actor）。</span>每一步，模型根据目标、历史与当前观测，从合法命令中选出下一步动作并执行。",
 "<span class=\"role-j\">Judge.</span> The model scores each action of a recorded trajectory. We vary what it sees, the trajectory up to the action (<em>Prefix</em>) or the whole trajectory (<em>Hindsight</em>), and what it is asked, whether the task will succeed after the action (<em>Value</em>) or whether the action helped achieve the goal (<em>Progress</em>).": "<span class=\"role-j\">裁判（Judge）。</span>模型为已有轨迹中的每个动作评分。实验调整两个维度：一是提供的上下文，即截至该动作的轨迹（<em>Prefix</em>，前缀）或完整轨迹（<em>Hindsight</em>，事后回看）；二是提问内容，即执行该动作后任务能否成功（<em>Value</em>），或该动作是否推进了目标（<em>Progress</em>）。",
 "<span class=\"role-t\">Teacher.</span> The model scores the actions of the policy being trained, and the scores enter GRPO as step-level credit. It stays frozen and is not used at test time.": "<span class=\"role-t\">教师（Teacher）。</span>模型为训练中的策略所执行的动作评分，分数作为步级信用信号接入 GRPO。模型参数始终冻结，测试阶段不参与。",
 "<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-1\">Figure 1</a> plays the three roles on the paper's running example: put a heated mug on a table.": "<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-1\">图 1</a>以论文的主线示例“把加热过的杯子放到桌上”依次演示三种角色。",
 "<span class=\"m1-tn\">1</span>Actor<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>": "<span class=\"m1-tn\">1</span>执行者<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>",
 "<span class=\"m1-tn\">2</span>Judge<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>": "<span class=\"m1-tn\">2</span>裁判<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>",
 "<span class=\"m1-tn\">3</span>Teacher<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>": "<span class=\"m1-tn\">3</span>教师<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>",
 "<b>Actor</b><span>picks the next action</span>": "<b>执行者</b><span>选择下一步动作</span>",
 "<b>Judge</b><span>scores a recorded action</span>": "<b>裁判</b><span>为已有轨迹中的动作评分</span>",
 "Recorded episode: put a heated mug in the cabinet": "历史回合：把加热过的杯子放进柜子",
 "<b>Teacher</b><span>scores the policy's own rollouts</span>": "<b>教师</b><span>为策略生成的 rollout 评分</span>",
 "Decision model": "决策模型",
 "question + context → typed answer. Here JEV, one of the six models we test.": "问题 + 上下文 → 固定格式的答案。示例模型为 JEV，即本文评测的六个模型之一。",
 "Choice probabilities": "各选项概率",
 "Easier subgoal first: the task is left incomplete.": "先完成了容易的子目标，导致任务失败。",
 "Same question; seeing the mug heated shows why it mattered.": "问题不变；看到后续的加热步骤后，才能判断这一步的作用。",
 "The no-op is pushed down; taking the cold mug back is credited.": "调低无效动作的优势，提高取回冷杯子一步的优势。",
 "<b>Figure 1.</b> One decision model, queried three ways on heated-mug tasks. <b>Actor:</b> JEV’s choice probabilities, averaged over 116 states in which the object still needs heating, cleaning or cooling. <b>Judge:</b> JEV’s score for step 9 of a recorded episode, seeing first the steps up to it and then the whole episode (paper Table 9). <b>Teacher:</b> illustrative scores from the paper’s Figure 1, centred within the group and added to GRPO’s outcome advantage. Use the tabs to jump to a role.": "<b>图 1：</b>同一决策模型在“加热杯子”类任务上的三种用法。<b>执行者：</b>JEV 在 116 个状态上的平均选项概率，这些状态中的物体均需先加热、清洗或冷却。<b>裁判：</b>JEV 对某一历史回合第 9 步的评分，分别提供截至第 9 步的轨迹与完整回合（论文表 9）。<b>教师：</b>分数为论文图 1 中的示意值，减去组内均值后加到 GRPO 的结果优势上。点击上方标签可切换角色。",
 "We evaluate six models that answer questions in this form. Three are released as <strong>dedicated decision models</strong> and are queried through their own decision APIs. The other three are <strong>general LLMs</strong> asked the same questions, either by prompting for a JSON answer or by reading the first-token probabilities of the valid answer labels. Two of these general LLMs are the base models of Decider v1.2 and GPT Decisions, so each dedicated model can be compared with its own base model.": "本文评测了六个支持此类问答的模型。其中三个是已正式发布的<strong>专用决策模型</strong>，通过各自的决策 API 调用；另外三个是<strong>通用大模型</strong>，提出相同问题后以两种方式获取答案：在提示中要求输出 JSON，或直接读取合法答案标签的首 token 概率。其中两个通用大模型分别是 Decider v1.2 与 GPT Decisions 的基座，因此这两个专用模型均可与各自的基座直接比较。",
 "Model": "模型",
 "Base LLM": "基座模型",
 "How the decision interface is obtained": "决策接口的实现方式",
 "Access": "访问方式",
 "undisclosed": "未公开",
 "API only": "仅 API",
 "full fine-tuning": "全参数微调",
 "open weights": "开放权重",
 "prompting (JSON answer)": "提示（输出 JSON）",
 "constrained readout (first-token probabilities)": "读取限定标签的概率（首 token）",
 "We use two text environments in which some requirements must be met in a fixed order. In <strong>ALFWorld</strong> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-alfworld\">[1]</a>, an agent completes household goals with commands such as <code>go to</code>, <code>take</code> and <code>heat</code>. Its <em>Clean</em>, <em>Heat</em> and <em>Cool</em> tasks have a dependency: the object's state must change before it is placed. <em>Pick2</em> also has two requirements, two objects to place, but they can be met in either order. In <strong>WebShop</strong> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-webshop\">[2]</a>, an agent searches a catalogue and must select the required options before it buys.": "实验采用两个文本环境，其中部分要求必须按固定顺序完成。<strong>ALFWorld</strong> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-alfworld\">[1]</a> 是家务环境，智能体使用 <code>go to</code>、<code>take</code>、<code>heat</code> 等命令完成目标。其中 <em>Clean</em>、<em>Heat</em>、<em>Cool</em> 三类任务存在依赖关系：物体须先改变状态，才能放到指定位置。<em>Pick2</em> 同样包含两个要求，即放置两个物体，但顺序不限。<strong>WebShop</strong> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-webshop\">[2]</a> 是购物环境，智能体在商品目录中搜索，下单前须选定指定选项。",
 "<span class=\"n\">2</span>As an actor, an easier subgoal gets in the way": "<span class=\"n\">2</span>作为执行者：容易的子目标导致决策偏离",
 "Finding 1": "发现 1",
 "As actors, all six models struggle when one subgoal must be completed before another: an easier subgoal draws them away from the one that has to come first.": "六个模型作为执行者时，只要某一子目标必须先于另一子目标完成，就容易出错：较容易的子目标使模型偏离应当先执行的步骤。",
 "Ordered subgoals are where acting breaks": "子目标有先后顺序时执行失败",
 "Every model succeeds far less often on tasks with a dependency than on tasks without one (<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-2\">Figure 2</a>). JEV completes 70.8% of <em>Pick2</em> tasks but at most 18.8% of each dependent task type. Decider v1.2, the strongest actor overall at 63.6%, completes only 18.8% of <em>Heat</em> tasks. Because <em>Pick2</em> also has two subgoals, the gap points to their <em>order</em> rather than their number as the difficulty.": "所有模型在有依赖任务上的成功率均远低于无依赖任务（<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-2\">图 2</a>）。JEV 能完成 70.8% 的 <em>Pick2</em> 任务，但在各类依赖任务上均不超过 18.8%。整体表现最好的执行者 Decider v1.2（63.6%）在 <em>Heat</em> 任务上也仅为 18.8%。<em>Pick2</em> 同样包含两个子目标，可见难点不在子目标的数量，而在其<em>顺序</em>。",
 "ALFWorld, acting": "ALFWorld，执行者",
 "Actor success rate by task type": "执行者在各类任务上的成功率",
 "All task types": "全部类型",
 "Pick2 vs dependent": "Pick2 与依赖任务",
 "<b>Figure 2.</b> Success rates (%) of the six models acting on ALFWorld, one run per task on the evaluation tasks later used for the trained policies. <i>Pick2</i> and the three dependent types both have two subgoals; only the dependent ones fix their order. Switch to “Pick2 vs dependent” to compare those directly; hover a cell for its value.": "<b>图 2：</b>六个模型在 ALFWorld 上作为执行者的成功率（%）。评估任务与后文策略训练所用任务相同，每个任务运行一次。<i>Pick2</i> 与三类依赖任务均包含两个子目标，区别在于只有依赖任务规定了顺序。切换至“Pick2 与依赖任务”可直接对比两者；鼠标悬停于格子上可查看具体数值。",
 "The failed episodes show how the order is broken. Holding the mug at the table, the actor can place it in one action, or walk to the microwave, heat it and come back. In many failures it places the unheated mug and the task can no longer be completed as intended.": "失败回合显示了顺序出错的过程。执行者手持杯子站在桌边，此时有两种选择：直接放下杯子，或前往微波炉加热杯子后再返回。许多失败回合中，执行者直接放下了未加热的杯子，此后任务无法按要求完成。",
 "Distraction, not ignorance": "错误源于干扰而非能力不足",
 "We collected 116 states, from 66 tasks, in which a single action would satisfy the easier subgoal while the required one was still unmet, and queried each actor there under two goals that differ only in the easier subgoal, for example “put a heated mug on the side table” versus “heat a mug”. Everything else, including the history, observation, candidate actions and remaining budget, is identical.": "从 66 个任务中选取 116 个状态。在这些状态下，一个动作即可完成容易的子目标，而必须先完成的子目标尚未完成。在每个状态上，分别用两个目标询问执行者，两者仅相差该容易的子目标，例如“把加热过的杯子放到边桌上”与“加热杯子”。其余输入完全相同，包括历史、观测、候选动作与剩余步数预算。",
 "<strong>With the full goal, JEV puts 63.8% of its probability on the easier subgoal and 14.6% on the step that must come first; without it, these become 2.5% and 77.6%</strong> (<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-3\">Figure 3</a>, left). All six actors shift the same way. They know the required step; the easier subgoal pulls probability away from it. Reminding them of the dependency barely helps: a generic hint changes success by −2.8 to +5.2 points, and adding a worked ordering example helps some models but not all (Figure 3, right).": "<strong>目标完整时，JEV 将 63.8% 的概率分配给容易的子目标，仅将 14.6% 分配给必须先执行的步骤；从目标中去掉容易的子目标后，两者变为 2.5% 与 77.6%</strong>（<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-3\">图 3</a> 左）。六个执行者的变化方向一致。由此可见，模型知道应先执行哪一步，只是概率被容易的子目标占据。提示模型注意依赖关系也几乎无效：加入一句通用提示后，成功率仅变化 −2.8 至 +5.2 个百分点；再提供一个按正确顺序完成的示例，也只对部分模型有效（图 3 右）。",
 "JEV, 116 states": "JEV，116 个状态",
 "Where the probability goes": "概率分配",
 "Share of JEV's probability by action type, %": "JEV 在各类动作上的概率占比（%）",
 "Full goal": "完整目标",
 "Without the easier subgoal": "去掉容易的子目标",
 "Same 116 states, continued to the end": "同一组 116 个状态，继续执行至回合结束",
 "Success with an ordering example in the prompt": "提示里加入顺序示例后的成功率",
 "Original prompt → hint plus a heated-mug example, %": "原提示 → 依赖提示 + 加热杯子示例（%）",
 "<b>Figure 3.</b> <b>Left:</b> JEV's action probabilities, grouped into the step toward the subgoal that must come first, the action that completes the easier subgoal, and everything else, with and without the easier subgoal in the goal. <b>Right:</b> success when each episode continues under the original prompt versus a dependency hint plus an ordering example. GPT Luna, which changes little, is omitted because the paper does not report its values in the text.": "<b>图 3：</b><b>左：</b>JEV 的动作概率，分为三组：走向必须先完成的子目标的动作、直接完成容易子目标的动作与其他动作；对比目标中包含与不包含容易子目标两种情况。<b>右：</b>各回合继续执行时的成功率，对比原提示与“依赖提示 + 顺序示例”。GPT Luna 变化很小，论文正文未给出具体数值，图中未绘出。",
 "Acting correctly here requires anticipating that the easy action leaves the task unfinished <em>before</em> any consequence is visible. A judge evaluates the action after its consequences have occurred, which is where the next section starts.": "执行者要在此处做对，必须在任何后果出现<em>之前</em>预见到：这一顺手的动作将导致任务无法完成。裁判则在后果出现之后评价动作。",
 "<span class=\"n\">3</span>As a judge, the question and the context decide": "<span class=\"n\">3</span>作为裁判：提问方式与可见信息的影响",
 "Finding 2": "发现 2",
 "The same models can recognise contributions they overlook as actors. Seeing the whole trajectory reveals how earlier actions feed later progress, and asking whether each action helped separates those actions from ones that change nothing.": "执行时被忽略的贡献，同一模型作为裁判时能够识别。只有看到完整轨迹，才能看出前期动作如何为后续进展铺垫；只有询问每个动作是否有帮助，才能将这些动作与未产生任何变化的动作区分开。",
 "We reused the successful continuations from the 116 states and asked each judge whether the first action taken from the diagnostic state helped achieve the goal, with outcome labels masked. Seeing the whole trajectory instead of the prefix raises the mean score of these actions for all six models; for JEV it goes from 0.41 to 0.59. That raises two questions: does a full trajectory simply make every action look good, and what does the judge actually gain from it?": "复用从上述 116 个状态出发的成功轨迹，隐去结果标签，询问每个裁判：在诊断状态下执行的第一个动作是否有助于达成目标。将前缀替换为完整轨迹后，六个模型对这些动作的平均评分均有所上升，JEV 由 0.41 升至 0.59。由此产生两个问题：完整轨迹是否只是让所有动作的评分普遍升高？裁判从中额外获得了哪些信息？",
 "Ask whether the action helped, not whether the task will succeed": "评估动作贡献而非任务成败",
 "We labelled actions in 462 ALFWorld trajectories as <em>milestones</em>, which achieve a subgoal, <em>no-ops</em>, which leave the environment unchanged, and <em>other</em>. With the whole trajectory visible, the <em>Value</em> question gives the three groups almost the same score: if the episode ends in success, every action in it “leads to success”. The <em>Progress</em> question spreads them apart for every model (<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-4\">Figure 4</a>). For JEV, within a trajectory, Progress scores milestones 0.36 above no-ops, against 0.05 for Value, and it ranks more milestones among each trajectory's top-scored actions, by 8.0 to 16.0 points.": "将 462 条 ALFWorld 轨迹中的动作标注为三类：<em>里程碑</em>，即完成某一子目标的动作；<em>无效动作</em>，即环境未发生任何变化的动作；以及<em>其他</em>动作。可见完整轨迹时，<em>Value</em> 问题对这三类动作的评分几乎相同：回合最终成功，其中每个动作都被视为“通向成功”。改用 <em>Progress</em> 问题后，六个模型均能区分三类动作（<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-4\">图 4</a>）。以 JEV 为例，在同一条轨迹内，Progress 对里程碑的评分比无效动作高 0.36，Value 仅高 0.05；在每条轨迹得分最高的动作中，Progress 选中里程碑的比例也高出 8.0 至 16.0 个百分点。",
 "ALFWorld, 462 trajectories, Hindsight context": "ALFWorld，462 条轨迹，完整轨迹（Hindsight）",
 "Mean action score by action type": "各类动作的平均得分",
 "<b>Figure 4.</b> Mean Hindsight scores for milestone, other and no-op actions under the two questions; scores are averaged within each trajectory, then across trajectories. The bracket shows the difference between the milestone and no-op means. Pick a judge to compare; Progress separates the groups for all six.": "<b>图 4：</b>两种问题下里程碑、其他与无效动作的 Hindsight 平均得分，先在每条轨迹内平均，再在轨迹间平均。括线标出里程碑与无效动作的均值差。切换裁判模型可以看到，在六个模型上，Progress 均能区分三组动作。",
 "Show the whole trajectory": "提供完整轨迹",
 "To see what the extra context buys, we held the question fixed to Progress and revealed the trajectory step by step: the prefix, then the immediate feedback after the action, then 25%, 50%, 75% and all of what follows. Over 167 trajectories, JEV's ranking of actions within a trajectory moves by 1.95 positions on average once feedback is added, and by 3.30 positions with the full trajectory. <a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-5\">Figure 5</a> shows one of them. Drag the slider, or press play.": "为分析额外上下文的作用，将问题固定为 Progress，并逐段展开轨迹：先只提供前缀，再加入动作之后的即时反馈，然后依次加入后续部分的 25%、50%、75% 与全部。在 167 条轨迹上，加入反馈后，JEV 对轨迹内动作的排名平均变动 1.95 位；看到完整轨迹时，平均变动 3.30 位。<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-5\">图 5</a> 展示其中一条轨迹，可拖动滑块或点击播放。",
 "JEV as a judge, Progress question": "JEV 作为裁判，Progress 问题",
 "“Put a heated mug in the cabinet”: scores as more of the episode becomes visible": "“把加热过的杯子放进柜子”：可见回合增加时各步得分的变化",
 "Visible context": "可见内容",
 "<b>Figure 5.</b> JEV's Progress scores for all 12 actions of one episode (paper Table 9). The mug is put in the cabinet before it is heated (step 6), taken back (7), heated in the microwave (8 to 10) and put back (12). Each bar is the score of that action when the judge sees the episode up to the action, plus the immediate feedback, plus 25%, 50%, 75% or all of the remaining steps.": "<b>图 5：</b>JEV 对同一回合全部 12 个动作的 Progress 评分（论文表 9）。该回合中，第 6 步将未加热的杯子放进柜子，第 7 步取回，第 8 至 10 步用微波炉加热，第 12 步放回柜子。每根柱子表示裁判对该动作的评分，裁判依次可见：截至该动作的回合，加入即时反馈，再加入后续步骤的 25%、50%、75% 或全部。",
 "Under the prefix, JEV rates the premature placement (step 6) at 0.79 and going to the microwave (8) and opening it (9) at only 0.23 and 0.20, the same preference for the easier subgoal that the actor showed. Immediate feedback makes it worse: placement rises to 0.90. Only as the continuation comes into view do the microwave steps earn credit; opening the microwave reaches 0.66 once heating is visible and 0.76 with the full trajectory. The repeated <code>look</code> (step 2) stays low throughout, because the prefix alone already shows that it repeats step 1.": "只看前缀时，JEV 对过早放置（第 6 步）评分 0.79，对走向微波炉（第 8 步）与打开微波炉（第 9 步）仅评 0.23 与 0.20，这与执行者偏向容易子目标属于同一问题。加入即时反馈后结果更差，放置的评分升至 0.90。随着后续步骤逐渐可见，微波炉相关步骤的评分才开始上升：看到加热步骤后，打开微波炉升至 0.66，看到完整轨迹时为 0.76。重复的 <code>look</code>（第 2 步）始终得分很低，因为仅凭前缀即可判断它重复了第 1 步。",
 "The two dedicated decision models whose base LLM is disclosed, Decider v1.2 and GPT Decisions, also judge more accurately than that base LLM given the same question, at 28% to 43% lower cost per score.": "Decider v1.2 与 GPT Decisions 公开了基座模型。对于相同问题，这两个专用决策模型作为裁判的准确性均高于各自的基座，每次评分的成本也低 28% 至 43%。",
 "<span class=\"n\">4</span>As a teacher, the best judge gives the best signal": "<span class=\"n\">4</span>作为教师：评判最准确的设置，训练效果也最好",
 "Finding 3": "发现 3",
 "The judgments that best separate useful from useless actions also train the strongest policies, and the gains are largest on the tasks the teacher fails as an actor.": "区分有用与无用动作效果最好的评分方式，训练出的策略也最强；提升最大的任务，恰恰是教师自身作为执行者时无法完成的任务。",
 "From scores to advantages": "从评分到优势",
 "GRPO gives every action in a rollout the same outcome advantage. For each task the policy samples a group of trajectories; after they finish, the teacher <span class=\"mi\">D</span> scores every executed action <span class=\"mi\">t</span> of every trajectory <span class=\"mi\">τ<sub>i</sub></span> from the goal and the trajectory alone, with no rewards, success labels or hidden state:": "GRPO 为一条 rollout 中的所有动作分配相同的结果优势。对每个任务，策略采样一组轨迹；轨迹结束后，教师 <span class=\"mi\">D</span> 仅依据目标与轨迹本身，为每条轨迹 <span class=\"mi\">τ<sub>i</sub></span> 中执行过的每个动作 <span class=\"mi\">t</span> 评分，不使用奖励与成功标签，也不访问隐藏状态：",
 "The scores are centred on the mean <span class=\"mi\">s̄</span> over all scored actions in the group and added with weight λ = 0.5. They are deliberately not divided by their standard deviation, so a group in which the teacher hardly distinguishes actions receives only small adjustments. <a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-6\">Figure 6</a> shows what the teacher term does to the two rollouts from Figure 1.": "分数先减去组内所有已评分动作的均值 <span class=\"mi\">s̄</span>，再乘以权重 λ = 0.5 加到优势上。此处有意不除以标准差：若教师在某一组内几乎无法区分动作优劣，该组获得的调整也相应较小。<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-6\">图 6</a> 展示了教师项对图 1 中两条 rollout 的影响。",
 "Illustrative group of two rollouts": "示意：同一组的两条 rollout",
 "What the teacher adds to each action's advantage": "教师项对各动作优势的调整量",
 "<b>Figure 6.</b> λ(<i>s</i> − <i>s̄</i>) for each action, using the illustrative teacher scores of Figure 1 (group mean 0.71). Bars above zero receive a larger advantage than GRPO alone would give, bars below a smaller one. The outcome advantage itself is the same for every action of a rollout, so only the teacher term distinguishes them. The paper trains with λ = 0.5.": "<b>图 6：</b>各动作的 λ(<i>s</i> − <i>s̄</i>)，教师分数取图 1 中的示意值，组均值为 0.71。柱子位于零线以上，表示该动作的优势高于单用 GRPO 时；位于零线以下则更低。同一条 rollout 中所有动作的结果优势相同，只有教师项能够区分这些动作。论文训练时取 λ = 0.5。",
 "Results": "实验结果",
 "We train Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct with JEV as the teacher under all four combinations of question and context, and compare against GRPO with outcome rewards alone (results from GiGPO <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-gigpo\">[3]</a>). Each policy is evaluated with three seeds. <strong>Hindsight + Progress gives the highest success on both environments: 72.8% → 82.9% on ALFWorld and 56.8% → 71.4% on WebShop.</strong> It improves on every ALFWorld task type, most on <em>Cool</em> (+23.0) and <em>Look</em> (+20.7). With the prefix only, the two questions perform about the same. The ordering matches the judge analysis: under Hindsight, the Value question gives every action of an episode nearly the same score and so says little about which actions helped.": "以 JEV 为教师训练 Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct，遍历问题与上下文的四种组合，基线为仅使用结果奖励的 GRPO，结果取自 GiGPO <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-gigpo\">[3]</a>。每个策略用三个随机种子评估。<strong>Hindsight + Progress 在两个环境上均最优：ALFWorld 成功率由 72.8% 提升至 82.9%，WebShop 由 56.8% 提升至 71.4%。</strong>ALFWorld 的每类任务均有提升，其中 <em>Cool</em>（+23.0）与 <em>Look</em>（+20.7）提升最大。仅提供前缀时，两种问题效果相当。这一排序与前文裁判分析的结论一致：在 Hindsight 设置下，Value 问题对同一回合内所有动作的评分相近，无法区分有用的动作。",
 "Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct, mean of three seeds": "Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct，三个种子的平均值",
 "Success rate, teacher-trained policy vs GRPO": "成功率：教师指导的策略与 GRPO 对比",
 "<span><i style=\"background:var(--base-2)\"></i>GRPO (outcome reward only)</span><span><i id=\"f7-key\" style=\"background:var(--tea)\"></i><span id=\"f7-name\">Hindsight + Progress</span></span><span>whiskers: ± std over seeds</span>": "<span><i style=\"background:var(--base-2)\"></i>GRPO（仅结果奖励）</span><span><i id=\"f7-key\" style=\"background:var(--tea)\"></i><span id=\"f7-name\">Hindsight + Progress</span></span><span>误差线：不同种子间的 ± 标准差</span>",
 "<b>Figure 7.</b> Success rates (%) of the 1.5B policy trained with JEV as the teacher under each question and context, against GRPO. The last two groups are overall ALFWorld success and WebShop success. Switch settings to compare; Hindsight + Progress is the best setting on both environments. The 7B option shows the same recipe on Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct.": "<b>图 7：</b>以 JEV 为教师、在不同问题与上下文设置下训练的 1.5B 策略的成功率（%），对照为 GRPO。最后两组分别为 ALFWorld 总体与 WebShop 的成功率。切换设置可以看到，Hindsight + Progress 在两个环境上均最优。选择 7B 可查看同一方法在 Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct 上的结果。",
 "The gain holds at 7B, from 77.6% to 83.8% on ALFWorld and from 66.1% to 73.6% on WebShop, and <strong>the 1.5B policy taught this way outperforms the 7B policy trained with outcome rewards alone on both environments.</strong> Hindsight + Progress also finishes sooner: it completes 74.5% of ALFWorld tasks within 20 actions, against 63.6% to 69.5% for the other settings, and 71.1% of WebShop tasks within 10 actions, against 60.9% to 62.2%.": "在 7B 规模上提升依然存在：ALFWorld 由 77.6% 提升至 83.8%，WebShop 由 66.1% 提升至 73.6%。<strong>以此方式训练的 1.5B 策略，在两个环境上均优于仅用结果奖励训练的 7B 策略。</strong>Hindsight + Progress 完成任务所需的步数也更少：ALFWorld 上 74.5% 的任务在 20 个动作以内完成，其他设置为 63.6% 至 69.5%；WebShop 上 71.1% 的任务在 10 个动作以内完成，其他设置为 60.9% 至 62.2%。",
 "Learning beyond the teacher": "学生超过教师",
 "On the same ALFWorld evaluation tasks, JEV completes 42.9% as an actor; the 1.5B policy trained on its scores completes 82.9%. <strong>The largest gains are on the dependent tasks, the ones JEV handles worst as an actor</strong>: there the policy reaches 86.8%, 6.9 to 16.2 points above the other question and context settings, while JEV itself completes only 14.7% of them (<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-8\">Figure 8</a>). The teacher does not need to solve a task to provide a useful signal for it.": "在同一批 ALFWorld 评估任务上，JEV 独立执行仅完成 42.9%，以其评分训练的 1.5B 策略完成 82.9%。<strong>提升最大的恰恰是 JEV 作为执行者时最不擅长的依赖任务</strong>：策略在这类任务上达到 86.8%，比其他问题与上下文设置高 6.9 至 16.2 个百分点，而 JEV 自身仅能完成其中的 14.7%（<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-8\">图 8</a>）。教师无法独立完成的任务，仍可由其提供有效的训练信号。",
 "ALFWorld, same evaluation tasks": "ALFWorld，同一批评估任务",
 "JEV acting vs the 1.5B policy JEV taught": "JEV 独立执行与其指导的 1.5B 策略对比",
 "<span><i style=\"background:var(--act)\"></i>JEV as actor</span><span><i style=\"background:var(--tea)\"></i>1.5B policy trained with JEV (Hindsight + Progress)</span>": "<span><i style=\"background:var(--act)\"></i>JEV 作为执行者</span><span><i style=\"background:var(--tea)\"></i>JEV 指导的 1.5B 策略（Hindsight + Progress）</span>",
 "<b>Figure 8.</b> Success rates (%) by task type. The arrow runs from JEV acting on its own (Table 2) to the policy it taught (Table 3). The policy surpasses its teacher everywhere except <i>Pick2</i>, and by the widest margins on the three dependent types.": "<b>图 8：</b>各类任务的成功率（%）。箭头由 JEV 独立执行的结果（表 2）指向其指导的策略（表 3）。除 <i>Pick2</i> 外，学生在所有类型上均超过教师，三类依赖任务上差距最大。",
 "<strong>Cost.</strong> We query JEV through OpenRouter at 0.042 USD per million input tokens to score every executed action during training: 150 steps, 16 tasks per batch, 8 rollouts per task. Scoring an entire training run costs between 22.21 and 30.07 USD.": "<strong>成本。</strong>训练中每个执行过的动作都需要评分。JEV 通过 OpenRouter 调用，输入价格为每百万 token 0.042 美元；训练共 150 步，每批 16 个任务，每个任务 8 条 rollout。一次完整训练的评分费用为 22.21 至 30.07 美元。",
 "Hindsight + Progress run": "Hindsight + Progress 训练",
 "Max actions per rollout": "每条 rollout 最多动作数",
 "Teacher API cost (USD)": "教师 API 费用（美元）",
 "<span class=\"n\">5</span>Takeaways for using decision models in agents": "<span class=\"n\">5</span>对智能体使用决策模型的启示",
 "<strong>Actors know the required step but are drawn to the easier one.</strong> They choose the right step when it is the only subgoal, and general reminders do not stop the error. When a decision model must act, restructuring the goal into ordered subgoals is more promising than adding instructions.": "<strong>执行者知道应执行哪一步，只是注意力被容易的步骤吸引。</strong>当必须先完成的步骤是唯一的子目标时，执行者能够选对；泛化的提醒无法纠正这一错误。若必须由决策模型执行，将目标拆分为有先后顺序的子目标，比增加指令更可能奏效。",
 "<strong>The question sets the granularity of the signal.</strong> Asking about the eventual outcome gives every action of a trajectory a similar score and largely repeats the outcome reward; asking about each action's contribution separates them.": "<strong>问题决定信号的粒度。</strong>询问最终结果时，轨迹中各动作的评分相近，基本等同于重复结果奖励；询问每个动作的贡献，才能区分这些动作。",
 "<strong>Hindsight targets the actor's own failure.</strong> Seeing the whole trajectory lets a judge credit the steps toward the subgoal that must come first. Decision models are best used to score actions after an episode, as in RL training, and are less suited to filtering actions online, where only the prefix exists.": "<strong>Hindsight 恰好针对执行者的出错之处。</strong>只有看到完整轨迹，裁判才能对走向必须先完成的子目标的步骤给予肯定。因此，决策模型最适合在回合结束后为动作评分，例如用于 RL 训练；不太适合在线筛选动作，因为此时只有前缀可用。",
 "<strong>Screen judges before training.</strong> Judging recorded trajectories identified the question and context that trained the best policy, at a small fraction of the cost of an RL run. Choose a teacher by how well it judges, not by how well it acts.": "<strong>训练前先选择裁判。</strong>仅在已有轨迹上比较评判效果，即可找到训练出最佳策略的问题与上下文组合，成本只占一次 RL 训练的一小部分。选择教师应依据其评判是否准确，而非其执行能力。",
 "<strong>Step-level supervision becomes affordable.</strong> A frozen decision model, queried after each episode and absent at test time, costs tens of dollars per run and lets a small policy outperform a larger one trained on outcomes alone.": "<strong>步级监督的成本不再高昂。</strong>决策模型参数冻结，仅在每个回合结束后调用，测试阶段无需使用。每次训练花费数十美元，即可使小规模策略超过仅用结果奖励训练的大规模策略。",
 "The full list of references, the prompts and the appendix experiments are in the <a class=\"tx\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.17167\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">paper</a>.": "完整参考文献、提示词和附录实验见<a class=\"tx\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.17167\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">论文</a>。",
 "Three robots in a watercolour landscape: an amber actor weighing which path to take, a blue judge inspecting footsteps with a magnifying glass, and a green teacher pointing at a board for a smaller student robot": "水彩风景中有三个机器人：琥珀色的执行者在两条路之间犹豫，蓝色的裁判手持放大镜查看脚印，绿色的教师指着黑板为一个小机器人讲课",
 "Role": "角色",
 "Show": "显示",
 "Goal": "目标",
 "Judge": "裁判",
 "s sub i t equals D of g, tau i, t, between 0 and 1; A sub i t equals A out plus lambda times s sub i t minus s bar": "s 下标 i t 等于 D 作用于 g、τ i、t，取值在 0 到 1 之间；A 下标 i t 等于 A out 加上 λ 乘以 s 下标 i t 减去 s 均值",
 "Teacher setting": "教师设置",
 "<a class=\"pill-btn solid\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.17167\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z\"></path><path d=\"M14 3v5h5M9 13h6M9 17h6\"></path></svg>Paper</a> <a class=\"pill-btn\" href=\"https://github.com/ZJU-REAL/decision-agents\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"m8 8-4 4 4 4M16 8l4 4-4 4\"></path></svg>Code</a> <a class=\"pill-btn\" href=\"https://zjureal.com/decision-agents/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"></circle><path d=\"M3 12h18M12 3a14 14 0 0 1 0 18M12 3a14 14 0 0 0 0 18\"></path></svg>Project page</a>": "<a class=\"pill-btn solid\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.17167\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z\"></path><path d=\"M14 3v5h5M9 13h6M9 17h6\"></path></svg>论文</a> <a class=\"pill-btn\" href=\"https://github.com/ZJU-REAL/decision-agents\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"m8 8-4 4 4 4M16 8l4 4-4 4\"></path></svg>代码</a> <a class=\"pill-btn\" href=\"https://zjureal.com/decision-agents/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"c